drift.rs is the ground truth for the drift engine's behavior — how the `links-reviewed:` epoch selects its certification commit, what classifies a link healthy/uncertified/broken/drifted/moved/unverifiable, and which outcomes `--fix` relocates versus skips. drift_relocation.rs pins that contract's relocation tiers and remedy texts as in-suite witness controls, so a change to the classification or skip semantics must keep them green; the anchor-contract explanation, the validate-and-fix skip procedure, and the diagnostics kind-and-exit-code tables describe that behavior for operators, so a change must also be re-verified against all three, and a doc that re-describes the contract must stay true of the implementation and of what the pins exercise. The doc side is authored as Eta templates because the rendered per-platform skill trees are generated output.
